## Classification

Industry practitioner risk-control taxonomy (not peer-reviewed academic literature) — a comprehensive enterprise risk register for "agentic AI" (multi-agent, tool-using, autonomous AI systems), structured as 5 risk categories → 30 named risks → 242 candidate controls, explicitly designed for integration into existing ISO/COSO/NIST enterprise risk management frameworks. Format B Wiki Intake Note — functions as a **control-taxonomy reference/checklist source** (S4/S6) rather than a theoretical or empirical contribution, but valuable as the most granular agentic-AI control inventory in the corpus to date.

